page DocsSettingsPassword

title "Password - Documentation"

template
<div class="min-h-[calc(100vh-4rem)] grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] bg-page transition-colors">

  <DocsSidebar active="settings-password" />

  <div class="min-w-0 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-10 py-6 sm:py-10">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">

    <article class="rounded-3xl border border-line bg-panel p-5 sm:p-8">
      <p class="text-zinc-500 text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] mb-3">Documentation / Settings</p>
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-light uppercase tracking-wide text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100">Password</h1>
      <p class="text-zinc-500 text-sm mt-2 mb-8">Change your password, or end every session on every device.</p>

      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">Change your password</h2>
      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">Open <strong>Settings</strong>, then <strong>Password</strong>. Fill in three fields and select <strong>Update password</strong>:</p>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line overflow-hidden mb-8">
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Current password</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">Your password today. Leaving it empty shows &ldquo;Enter your current password.&rdquo;</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">New password</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">At least 10 characters, with a letter, a number and a symbol. It must be different from your current password.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Confirm new password</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">The same new password again.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">While you type</h2>
      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">Once you start typing a new password, a strength bar appears with a label, and four checks tick off as you meet them: <strong>10+ characters</strong>, <strong>A letter</strong>, <strong>A number</strong> and <strong>A symbol</strong>. Under the confirm field the page says &ldquo;Passwords match.&rdquo; or &ldquo;Passwords don't match yet.&rdquo;.</p>
      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-8">The <strong>Show</strong> button on any of the three fields reveals all three at once. Select <strong>Hide</strong> to cover them again.</p>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border-l-2 border-l-brand-500 bg-brand-500/5 px-4 py-3 mb-8">
        <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">After a successful change you are signed out everywhere, this device included, and taken to the login page. Log in again with the new password.</p>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">Sign out everywhere</h2>
      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">This ends every session on every device, including the one you are using. Use it if you think someone else has access to your account.</p>
      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-8">Select <strong>Sign out everywhere</strong>, then <strong>Yes, sign me out</strong> to confirm, or <strong>Cancel</strong> to back out. You land on the login page.</p>
      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">If something goes wrong</h2>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line overflow-hidden mb-8">
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Password must be 10 or more characters with a letter, a number and a symbol.</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">The new password does not meet the rules. Check the four ticks.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Your new password must be different from the current one.</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">Choose a password you have not just used.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Passwords don't match.</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">The confirm field differs from the new password.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">A message under Current password</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">The current password was not accepted. Re-enter it and try again.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Couldn't change your password.</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">Something failed on our side. Your password is unchanged. Try again.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Couldn't sign you out.</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">The sessions were not ended. Try Sign out everywhere again.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 mt-8 pt-5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
        <a href="/docs/settings/members" class="text-sm text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-500 hover:underline">&larr; Members</a>
        <a href="/docs/settings/two-factor" class="text-sm text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-500 hover:underline">Two-factor &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </article>

  </div>
  </div>
</div>
